{"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "What's the difference between population and sample standard deviation in numpy?"}, {"role": "silicat", "content": "By default numpy computes population std (ddof=0). Set `ddof=1` for the sample standard deviation.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndata = np.array([2, 4, 4, 4, 5, 5, 7, 9])\nprint(data.std())          # population, ddof=0\nprint(data.std(ddof=1))    # sample, ddof=1\n```"}]}
